Things to know:
  - protected in method, variable and attributes (class cannot be protected)
      -> protected methodes and variables can only be accessed by Class, Packages and Subclasses(doesn't matter if same/different package)
  - final in class, method, variable and attributes
      -> final variable/ attribute: to create a constant (invariant value)
      -> final method: cannot be overridden by subclasses
      -> final classes: cannot be inherited
  - static in class, method, variable
      -> static variable: static variable are commonly shared across all instances of a class
      -> static methods: methods that are useful even without interaction with Object (https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2671496/java-when-to-use-static-methods)
      -> static classes: 
  - Map, HashMap Class (from java.util.Map & java.util.HashMap)
  - List Class (from java.util.List)
  - what is Enum ?  
  - concept of Immutability in Java (with objects etc.)
